  Libraries bundled in the TYPO3 archives
    Each under its own licence, shipped with its source in the archive and,
    unmodified, in the image. Each stack's LICENCES.md lists the licence
    files its release bundles, for example 6.2/LICENCES.md. The image has
    it at /usr/share/doc/typo3-<version>/LICENCES.md.

  Both inventories are generated from the archives by
  .github/scripts/licence_inventory.py, and CI fails when they are stale.

Images this project copies unchanged into ghcr.io/mteu/typo3-throwback/

  mysql (5.5), nginx (1.27.5), debian (bullseye, bullseye-slim) and
  php (5.6-apache) are copies of the upstream Docker Official Images, pinned
  by digest. Their contents carry their upstream licences, for example
  GPL-2.0 for MySQL Community Server and for many Debian packages, and the
  PHP License for PHP. The upstream projects publish the source. For Debian
  packages it is on archive.debian.org and snapshot.debian.org.

Packages the builds install

  The typo3 and php4-base images add Debian packages, such as libfaketime,
  ImageMagick and the gd development files. Each stays under its Debian
  licence. Debian publishes the source of every package.

  The WebAssembly site installs sql.js from npm, pinned in
  wasm/package-lock.json. sql.js is MIT-licensed. The SQLite it
  compiles is in the public domain. The WebAssembly builds link Emscripten's
  runtime and C library, which are MIT- and University of Illinois/NCSA-
  licensed, with musl under the MIT licence. For GD they also link
  Emscripten's ports of zlib (zlib licence), libpng (libpng licence),
  libjpeg 9f (the Independent JPEG Group's licence) and FreeType (the
  FreeType License), and the GD 2.0.28 bundled in PHP keeps its own
  licence. So does the expat 1.95.6 bundled in PHP, which is
  MIT-licensed; PHP's archive leaves out its licence file, so
  wasm/php-4.4.9/expat-COPYING carries it. Its checks also install
  Playwright, which is Apache-2.0-licensed and is not published.

The site published to GitHub Pages

  .github/workflows/pages.yml publishes PHP 4.4.9 compiled to WebAssembly,
  sql.js and the TYPO3 3.3.0 and 3.8.1 archives. Each archive bundles a
  phpMyAdmin, under the GPL. The site carries LICENSES.txt with the notices
  the PHP License and the Zend Engine License require, the credit lines the
  libjpeg and FreeType licences require, the licence files in each TYPO3
  archive, and the full texts of every licence above that applies to it.

